  "id": "rickets",
  "term": "rickets",
  "definition": "Rickets is a group of disorders in which the growing skeleton does not mineralize properly at the growth plates and in bone tissue. It can be acquired, such as from too little vitamin D or calcium, or inherited, and it often involves low calcium and/or phosphorus levels along with bone deformities and sometimes muscle weakness, tetany, convulsions, or laryngospasm.",
